WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.183
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.183 --> 00:00:11.169
Last time our show got its voice.

5
00:00:11.169 --> 00:00:12.734
Now it gets its first job.

6
00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:16.766
Today is quests: what they're made of, how Voyage knows one's done,

7
00:00:16.766 --> 00:00:21.219
and the bit that trips everyone up, how a quest actually reaches a player.

8
00:00:22.633 --> 00:00:24.367
Open Story, then Quests.

9
00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:29.713
Every quest in your world sits in this list, and you click one to open it.

10
00:00:29.713 --> 00:00:33.686
Here's the show's first job: The Lion's Gone Walkabout.

11
00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:37.470
The quest statement is the situation that starts it all.

12
00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:43.131
Bramble, our ancient, half-blind lion, slipped his cage, and the whole town is losing its mind.

13
00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:47.285
The main objective is the goal players see in their quest log.

14
00:00:47.285 --> 00:00:48.664
Write it like an order.

15
00:00:48.664 --> 00:00:52.622
Find Bramble and get him back in his cage before the sheriff does.

16
00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:56.332
The completion condition is how Voyage knows it's done.

17
00:00:56.332 --> 00:01:01.022
Write what done looks like in plain words, and Voyage watches the story for it.

18
00:01:01.022 --> 00:01:04.050
Studio even turns it into a hidden trigger for you.

19
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.228
Detailed means it happens at a place you pick.

20
00:01:07.228 --> 00:01:09.838
We don't have any places yet, so it's blank,

21
00:01:09.838 --> 00:01:13.219
and Voyage skips the travel and goes straight to the job.

22
00:01:13.219 --> 00:01:15.413
It gets a real place in episode five.

23
00:01:15.867 --> 00:01:18.388
Quest source is who the job comes from.

24
00:01:18.388 --> 00:01:20.069
Old Marla, the lion tamer.

25
00:01:20.533 --> 00:01:22.952
The design brief is just for the narrator.

26
00:01:22.952 --> 00:01:24.161
Players never see it.

27
00:01:24.161 --> 00:01:29.113
Mine says laughs first, the sheriff's the real danger, and nobody wins it on one roll.

28
00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:33.932
And status. Hidden means nobody has this quest yet.

29
00:01:35.333 --> 00:01:36.477
Detailed or basic?

30
00:01:36.477 --> 00:01:38.827
Detailed happens at a place you pick.

31
00:01:38.827 --> 00:01:43.019
Basic lets Voyage make up the place, somewhere nearby or far away.

32
00:01:43.019 --> 00:01:47.846
Voyage's guide says only detailed quests check their done line on their own,

33
00:01:47.846 --> 00:01:51.657
but I tested it, and basic ones get the same hidden trigger.

34
00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:54.822
The rest of the form, quickly.

35
00:01:54.822 --> 00:01:57.864
Objectives is an optional checklist players can see.

36
00:01:57.864 --> 00:02:00.029
Next step is a hint shown to players.

37
00:02:00.029 --> 00:02:03.364
Conclusive means finishing this quest ends its story arc.

38
00:02:03.364 --> 00:02:08.864
And on complete effects is what happens the moment it's done, like handing out the next quest.

39
00:02:08.864 --> 00:02:10.795
We'll use that one with triggers.

40
00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.261
Here's the bit that trips everyone up.

41
00:02:14.261 --> 00:02:17.134
A quest sitting in this list does nothing on its own.

42
00:02:17.134 --> 00:02:19.086
It only reaches a player three ways.

43
00:02:19.086 --> 00:02:21.689
A story start hands it out when the game begins.

44
00:02:21.689 --> 00:02:23.804
A trigger hands it out partway through.

45
00:02:23.804 --> 00:02:26.515
Or another quest hands it on when that one's done.

46
00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:28.900
That's quests.

47
00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:34.002
The lion job is linked in the description if you want to paste it into a test world.

48
00:02:34.002 --> 00:02:37.890
Next time is episode three, and the one after: narrative events,

49
00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.137
story beats Voyage plays out for you.

50
00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:44.548
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

